Fix several issues in the C++ backend: datatype values print as `Typename.Ctor(fields)` (previously `print` of a datatype failed to compile), sets, maps, and tuples print with the same braces and separators as the other backends (`{a, b}`, `map[k := v]`, `(a, b)`), 8-bit integers print as numbers instead of characters, map literals with a duplicate key keep the last value, and codatatypes are rejected as unsupported instead of crashing the compiler.
